    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d189">

                <pb facs="0344" n="230" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg230"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.00 R 294/84</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Child</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rome</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1922-05-22"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">May 22, 1922</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 320</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to enclose herewith
                    translation of a <hi rendition="#italic">Note Verbale</hi> dated May 15th from
                    the Italian Foreign Office, in reply to the representations made in accordance
                    with your instructions in regard to the reimbursement of the expenses of the
                    American Army of Occupation.</p>
                <p>It will be noted that, as reported in confidential telegram No. 72 of May 8, 2
                        p.m.,<anchor n="66" xml:id="d189-f1"/> the objections of the Italian
                    Treasury have been omitted from the text of the reply.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Richard Washburn
                    Child</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d189-a1.xml" xpointer="d189-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
